say which text storage got the text

edited:range:changeInLength: is the funnel every mutation of every NSTextStorage goes through, so
one line here answers a question that took several rounds otherwise: a text view drawing len=0 has
either been given nothing at all, or been pointed at a DIFFERENT storage from the one the
application filled. Only the pointer separates those, and nothing printed it.

Measured on iA Writer, whose editor pane is blank. In one run, 875 edits, ALL of them to a single
storage, and it is not the editor's:

  CIDER_TEXTEDIT NSTextStorage_concrete(0x7c5f54cabaf0) mask=0x3 range=0+0 delta=4 len=4
  CIDER_TEXTEDIT NSTextStorage_concrete(0x7c5f54cabaf0) mask=0x3 range=0+9 delta=-9 len=0
  CIDER_TEXTDRAW IAEditorTextView ... storage=NSTextStorage_concrete_Aspects_(0x7c5f54cc4390) len=0

The edited one is cleared and refilled with short strings and never exceeds 113 characters, which is
the shape of a shared field editor measuring cell text rather than a document. The editor's own
storage receives ZERO edits in the whole run.

So the document text never reaches ANY text storage. On CIDER_TRACE_TEXT, beside the draw, adopt and
insert lines already there.

--- a/AppKit/NSTextView.subproj/NSTextStorage.m
+++ b/AppKit/NSTextView.subproj/NSTextStorage.m
@@ -224,6 +224,16 @@
                  range: (NSRange) range
         changeInLength: (int) delta
 {
+    /* EVERY MUTATION OF EVERY TEXT STORAGE goes through here, so this says which storage got text and
+     * which did not. A text view that draws len=0 has either been given nothing, or been pointed at a
+     * different storage from the one the application filled, and the POINTER is what separates
+     * those. Task #194. */
+    if (getenv("CIDER_TRACE_TEXT") != NULL && getenv("CIDER_TRACE_TEXT")[0] != (char) 0) {
+        fprintf(stderr, "CIDER_TEXTEDIT %s(%p) mask=0x%x range=%lu+%lu delta=%d len=%lu\n",
+                object_getClassName(self), self, editedMask, (unsigned long) range.location,
+                (unsigned long) range.length, delta, (unsigned long) [self length]);
+        fflush(stderr);
+    }
 
     if (_beginEditing == 0) {
         _editedMask = editedMask;
